This is a PROTOTYPE, not real content. gen-site.php only loads files
whose name ends in exactly ".entry" — this one ends in ".entry.example",
so it is never loaded, validated, or rendered. It exists purely so a
human (or a content-generation tool) has a blank, all-fields-shown copy
to start from.

To use it:
  1. Copy this file to a new name ending in ".entry", following this
     type's naming convention (see the heading below).
  2. Delete this whole instructional block, including the line of
     dashes, so the file starts with "+++" on the very first line.
  3. Fill in the fields. Leave optional ones blank (or delete the line
     entirely) if they don't apply.
  4. See CONTENT-GUIDE.md for what every field actually does.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Event — one flat folder for both event types (a workshop and a retreat
share this exact same shape, distinguished only by the `type` field
below, which is `workshop` in this copy — change it to `retreat` for
one); a filename that sorts the way you want it to read, e.g.
"2025-11-creativity-writing-intensive.entry".

+++
title:
domain:
coaches:
type: workshop
date:
format:
location:
booking_link:
summary:
+++

The full description, shown only on the event's own page. To embed a
photo of the venue (in-person events only): a plain
<img src="../img/your-photo.jpg" alt="Describe what's in the photo"
class="content-photo content-photo-left"> tag written directly here —
content-photo-left or content-photo-right, and more than one is fine for
a longer description (alternate sides). If your description opens with
one, set an explicit summary above instead of relying on the
first-sentence fallback.
